  "novelty": "NONE CLAIMED. Curriculum and transfer learning own the question of whether earlier training makes later training cheaper; catastrophic forgetting and negative transfer own the risk side. The contribution is the RECEIPT DISCIPLINE -- a reset arm, a clairvoyant parent, a task-specific bound, attributable reuse witnesses, and a registered kill criterion -- applied to a transition that is otherwise ordinary.",
  "plan": {
    "capability_gate": "D1 correctness is NOT 1.0 by construction -- an arm that applies a rule to an exception answers wrongly. Work is compared only between arms at matched correctness, and where correctness differs the comparison is reported as INADMISSIBLE rather than as a win. This is the first experiment in the programme where the gate can actually bind on the machine under test.",
    "constitution": "SzeChunYiu/ORION-OCM#144",
    "contribution_level": "L1",
    "costs": {
      "apply": 10,
      "compose": 5,
      "composite_bits": 48,
      "derive": 100,
      "exception_rate": 0.1,
      "fact_bits": 8,
      "induce": 40,
      "k_induce": 3,
      "lookup": 1,
      "rule_bits": 32,
      "verify": 25
    },
    "decisive_causal_question": "CONTINUED_OCM versus RESET_OCM. The two are the same code, the same budget, the same D1 stream, and the same immutable architecture. They differ in exactly one bit: whether the D0 store crosses the boundary. Any D1 work difference between them is caused by the crossing or by nothing.",
    "depends_on": "results/RETAIN_E10_V1.json",
    "evidence_class": "E2",
    "kill_criterion": "If CONTINUED_OCM does not beat RESET_OCM on D1-only work at matched correctness, there is no D0 to D1 transition here. The spine's first entry is then a REFUSAL, recorded with the same weight as a success would have been.",
    "novelty": "NONE CLAIMED. Curriculum and transfer learning own the question of whether earlier training makes later training cheaper; catastrophic forgetting and negative transfer own the risk side. The contribution is the RECEIPT DISCIPLINE -- a reset arm, a clairvoyant parent, a task-specific bound, attributable reuse witnesses, and a registered kill criterion -- applied to a transition that is otherwise ordinary.",
    "predictions_frozen_before_execution": {
      "Q1": "CONTINUED_OCM beats RESET_OCM on D1-only work at matched correctness.",
      "Q2": "The advantage is attributable: the reused base rules that fire in D1 are named, and removing them from the carried store removes the advantage.",
      "Q3": "CONTINUED_OCM does NOT beat STRONG_ADAPTIVE_PARENT, which sees the future. If it does, the parent is implemented wrongly and the run is void.",
      "Q4": "CONTINUED_OCM's advantage over RESET_OCM SHRINKS as D1 lengthens, because a reset arm re-earns the same rules. Registered in this direction so that a shrinking advantage is a confirmed prediction and not a discovered excuse.",
      "Q5": "Carrying state carries risk: CONTINUED_OCM's harmful-transfer exposure is at least RESET_OCM's, because it holds more rules to misapply. If it is lower, the exception mechanism is not biting and the run is uninformative."
    },
    "prior_information_audit": {
      "CONTINUED_OCM": "its own D0 store, earned by paying for every derivation in it",
      "RESET_OCM": "nothing from D0; identical architecture and identical D1 stream",
      "STRONG_ADAPTIVE_PARENT": "D0 and D1 and the whole future",
      "TASK_SPECIFIC_OCM": "D1 only, and a representation chosen for D1's composites",
      "exceptions": "no arm is told which answers are exceptions; every arm may pay VERIFY_COST to find out, and every arm is charged the same for it"
    },
    "programme": "SzeChunYiu/ORION-OCM#151",
    "scaling_relevance": "D1 length and store budget are both swept. The developmental claim is that the D1-only advantage does not vanish as D1 grows, because a reset arm eventually re-earns everything; if the advantage decays to zero the transition is a STARTUP EFFECT and must be reported as one.",
    "scientific_question": "Does prior D0 competence, carried across a stage boundary under a bounded and priced store, causally make D1 competence cheaper -- at matched correctness, and against a reset arm with the same architecture and the same D1 information?",
    "strongest_parent_attack": "STRONG_ADAPTIVE_PARENT sees D0 and D1 concatenated and the entire future demand stream, and keeps the mixed instance-and-rule set a clairvoyant would keep. It has strictly more information than the lineage. E10 already established that the arm does NOT beat this parent, and DEV-1 does not expect to either; the parent is here to bound the claim, not to be beaten.",
    "study_id": "DEV1_D0_TO_D1_V1",
